  "status_text": "At least 54 lights have to turn back on somewhere if only two gates can flip bits. Lean checked the bound for fitting circuits of AND, OR and NOT gates with at most two input wires each, on 23 dots with one light per eight-dot group. A light must be on if its group misses all chosen groups, and off if its own group is chosen. With at most two NOTs, two disjoint parts cover at least 19 dots and every eight-dot group within either part names a light that rises somewhere as choices grow. The smallest possible count of groups on those parts is 9+45=54 (L-lib-1277).",
